---
description: Use for Nuxt Content collections, content files, frontmatter fields, or collection queries. Do not use for non-content UI or server-route changes.
globs:
  - "content/**/*"
  - "content.config.ts"
  - "app/pages/**/*.vue"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Define every new content field in the owning collection's `schema` in
  `content.config.ts` before adding it to a content file. Nuxt Content uses a
  collection schema for validation and TypeScript inference.
- Keep a field's validation, type, query use, and content fixture aligned; add
  a focused test when the contract has executable behaviour.
- Preserve a collection's explicit source boundary. Make each document match
  one collection, or define an explicit exclusion strategy before overlap.
- Reference: https://content.nuxt.com/docs/collections/define
